From ad8691de78d36b4531e9e7b42993bd7983f2cb90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Gregory <allengregoryiv@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:17:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ThriftyCam (05c8:0a00, USB 3) as a native camera: 1600x1304
 MJPEG 60 fps, named and matched by USB port

- NativeCameraSource: 05c8:0a00 joins the default verified IDs (Thriftiest, Swyft). It has no serial, so it keeps
  its by-path uniquePath (e.g. platform-xhci-hcd.0-usb-0:1:1.0), the same at SuperSpeed and high speed.
- PVUsbCameraInfo.humanReadableName: a ThriftyCam is named by model and port, "ThriftyCam_xhci0-1", so two of
  them get different stable names (the cscore name is just "PC Camera").
- QuirkyCamera: ThriftyCam with Gain and MJPEGOnly (its YUYV modes are slower or don't stream).
- Camera delay per model: ThriftyCam 0.7 ms exposure end -> first packet, PTS delay 0 (assumed: its PTS is
  ~0.7 ms before the first packet; no LED test yet). A bare SPECTRUM_CAMERA_DELAY_US number stays the other
  cameras' default; a key=value naming the camera still overrides.
- AprilTagPipeline: solvePNP needs a calibration; a camera without one (a new ThriftyCam) publishes 2D targets
  instead of a NullPointerException every frame.

Bench Pi 5, three cameras native at once (30 s): Thriftiest 121.2 fps capture->publish p50/p99 8.91/10.32 ms,
Swyft 120.0 fps 9.19/17.81, ThriftyCam 60.2 fps 16.76/20.56; PhotonVision 184% of a core. ThriftyCam usbreset
x3: back in 0.54-0.56 s at 60 fps, SuperSpeed, controls kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
